        },
        "subject": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for lod mirror staleness/fill logic",
        "message": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for lod mirror staleness/fill logic\n\nExport lod_last_non_stale_mirror(), lod_fill_mirrors(), lod_lu_ops,\nlod_prepare_resync() and lod_prepare_resync_mirror() for direct\ntesting, without a mounted filesystem or OSD/OSP.\n\nAdd lustre/kunit/lod_mirror_test.c covering lod_last_non_stale_mirror()\n(refusing to stale a mirror if that would stale every mirror, across\none/two/three mirrors - complements sanity-ec.sh 100a/100b),\nlod_fill_mirrors() (parsing ldo_comp_entries[] into ldo_mirrors[]:\nstale propagation, LCME_FL_PREF_WR vs. non-rotational fallback,\nmixed parity/non-parity and HSM components, mismatched mirror id\ncounts - more exhaustive than the sanity-ec 2b/2c and sanity 90a/90b\nit complements, since it reaches branches that would otherwise need\ncrafted layouts and failure injection), and lod_prepare_resync()/\nlod_prepare_resync_mirror() (deciding which not-yet-inited components\nof a stale or named mirror need instantiating for a resync).\n\nmirror_test_setup() and friends: memset() zeroed the already\ninitialized mtc_env, corrupting lc_remember and LBUG-ing in\nlu_context_fini() on module exit. Use\noffsetof(struct mirror_test_ctx, mtc_env) as the memset length.\n\nresync_test_setup(): allocate lti_comp_idx with\nOBD_ALLOC_PTR_ARRAY() instead of pointing it at a struct-embedded\narray, since lod_key_fini() unconditionally frees it with\nOBD_FREE_PTR_ARRAY(), which otherwise corrupts the slab allocator.\n\nRun from sanity test_51l, loading kunit on the MDS with enable=1.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5\nChange-Id: I6f31f5d25fe3a20fe4d1a4b7e0dce9d626d0775e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
